  "title": {
    "rendered": "One Day From Tomorrow"
  },
  "content": {
    "rendered": "\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">People are always amazed when I share from the stage that it took me four decades to fully embrace my calling within this journey called life.&nbsp; I too am amazed yet not surprised that it took so long for me to understand this process known as purpose.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Purpose is one of those terms that takes on whatever definition we need it to represent depending on what we are or are not accomplishing at any given moment in time.&nbsp; What I mean by that is this; when things are moving along at a steady and measurable state, I am completely content to settle back within the arms of purpose and enjoy the ride.&nbsp; However, when things are not moving along at what I would deem a steady and measurable state…, I quickly begin fretting over what I must have done wrong, or what I could have done better.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Why is it that when the ebb and flow of life gets our shoes wet simply because we did not retreat towards the shore of safety quickly enough, we immediately lose the respect for the beauty of that same ebb and flow as it pertains to our lives when we purposely allow those same waters to freely splash over our bare feet?</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It is my opinion, at least within my own experiences; that we see whatever it is <em>we choose</em> to see, we feel whatever it is <em>we choose</em> to feel, and we experience whatever it is <em>we choose</em> to experience.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">I have been an avid believer for quite some time now, that there truly are no mistakes within our journeys, only miracles in the making.&nbsp; It was not until I was nearly 50 years old that this mindset began to take hold, and once it did…, my purpose became clearer with each passing test.&nbsp; Notice that I stated <strong><em>passing</em></strong> tests, meaning those tests that I actually passed…, those moments when simple ‘experiences’ became <strong><em>learning</em></strong> experiences.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For many years I was missing the purpose which was the learning found deep within that gooey-chewy center of every experience I had ever been made to live.&nbsp; I chose to believe for the first forty odd years of my life, that any and everything that was different than what I saw as “normal” was some curse or punishment for something I must have done to offend the Universe.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">&nbsp;Granted, much of this defeatist mindset was created within my childhood parameters of belief due to no fault of my own.&nbsp; Afterall, I <strong><em>did not choose</em></strong> to be given away by my birth mother after a few days of life, I <strong><em>did not choose</em></strong> for my adoptive mother to suddenly die while I was still just a young boy, I also <strong><em>did not choose</em></strong> to spend the majority of my remaining childhood years bouncing between 20 other homes, but nonetheless…it happened.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The turning of the tide in life begins the moment we begin to not only choose, but to embrace that truth which makes the choosing much more simplistic; the truth that all things work together for our overall good in the end.&nbsp; Once I began to understand that it was my choice to continue living or not within my world of yesterdays, it was then and only then that I began to muster the courage to glance in the opposite direction…towards my tomorrows.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">So many dreams and opportunities are lost simply because we write our future hopes and goals on an unrealistic calendar, that calendar which promises to never move towards the here and now, the calendar known as either <strong>someday or one day.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Why are we so willing, so adamant and determined to remain rooted in our pains of yesterday?&nbsp; Why is it that we relish so often the glorifying of those moments of our past that have caused us the most grief and despair, yet are so unwilling to invest that same amount of energy in the belief or faith that tomorrow is why we were made to live those yesterdays in the first place?</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The answer has always been, is still today, and will forever more… be the same; it is always about the <strong><em>learning</em></strong> within every experience.&nbsp; When we have learned, we have also earned.&nbsp; We have earned all the promise that a new tomorrow holds within its grasp, we have earned yet another opportunity to take what we have today and make it even better.&nbsp; We have earned another opportunity to leave every person and each experience we encounter, better than the way we originally found them.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It is true, we choose; in everything…we choose.&nbsp; We choose our way into situations, (some good and some not-so-good) and we either choose our way out…or not.&nbsp; We can choose to remain within the test or choose to pass the test.&nbsp; We can choose to remain within the confines of those yesterdays that do not even belong to us, or we can choose to learn towards our very own unique tomorrows.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Whatever your choice may be, never forget that through it all no matter how it looks, no matter how it feels…we are always only one day from tomorrow, one day away from another world of wonderful choices, so choose won’t you please?</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Xoxo</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Loren</p>\n",
    "protected": false
  },
